bd26fb1f59fff4c324a2581b148ae054bc01ed56perf(apfs): line copies clone hard-linked files one by one instead of copying the whole tree (#355)

* perf(apfs): a tree with hard links is cloned by folders; only the linked files are copied one by one

clone_complete copied the whole tree file by file when one file of it had a second link,
so its links stayed links. One hard link in a large ignored folder (Attar: chromium/ 70 GB
and .attar-cache/ 30 GB) made an automatic save take more than ten minutes. Now the
folders above the linked files are walked, each linked file is copied by itself with one
map of inodes, and every other subtree is one clone. On APFS one folder clone of 20k files
takes 0.75 s, a file-by-file copy 5.6 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jp3rumuJHd1FeTnGGzzrED

* fix(apfs): seal the linked files of a read-only copy after the walk

A link to a file that is immutable already cannot be made: the second link of a group
failed with 'Operation not permitted' (thin tests). The flags of the linked files are now
set after every link exists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jp3rumuJHd1FeTnGGzzrED

* fix(apfs): a folder that a writer removed during a copy is skipped when the copy gets its folder times

The copy of a tree with hard links now goes through the folder clone, which then gives the
folders the times of the scan. A folder that a writer removed after the scan is not in the
copy: the times step failed with 'No such file or directory'. It skips such a folder, as
the copy does; the scan after the copy sees the change. The re-copy loop names its last
error.

