eaa67f655a8f171f6b3a936694d578b183684dc8fix(remote): a chunk pack whose data is gone counts as absent, and the sweep deletes its index (#360)

A pack index without its data (a delete that removed the data and not the index) made the
next push stop ('has an index but no data') when a chunk of it was dead, and otherwise a
new cache reused its chunks, so no machine could read that cache. A pack now counts only
with both objects: a push uploads such chunks again, and every sweep pass deletes the
index without data. release goes on past a pack whose data went during the pass.


