f9667151a34d8871949008c22787c83a032411b5fix(remote): index write takes no project lock, writes the heads first and goes on past an unreadable tree (#359)

layr index write held the project lock while it read every tree of the store: more than ten
minutes on project layr, and every command of the project waited. It only reads the records
and writes create-only remote objects, so it takes no lock now. The heads snapshot goes up
first: a run that failed in the paths phase left a store without heads, and the site then
read every record segment (14 to 25 s). A tree that cannot be read marks its state as
unavailable, names it, and the index goes on.


