e72c6aaa87898ceeac01b87d1ae68916c1c580cdfix(privs): a command of the caller runs with the caller's PATH, and init --from-git names the git error (#354)

command_as gave every child the fixed PATH /usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin. An old Intel
/usr/local/bin/git does not run on Apple silicon without Rosetta, so init --from-git said
'is not a Git checkout' for every checkout. A command of the caller's own process now uses
the caller's PATH; a service (root for a user) uses a fixed PATH with /opt/homebrew/bin
first on macOS. init --from-git adds the git error to its message.


