b182e74cfc99d9bd949926fb31fab94b9a763b52fix(trust): check the whole record of a limited machine and drop trusts of untrusted signers (#352)

* fix(trust): check the whole record of a limited machine and drop trusts of untrusted signers

A cache writer's record was judged by its op only, but Db::derive applies the
states, line moves and some data keys of a record of any op. A writer's config
record could make a source state or move a line. Now Terms::refusal gets the
record's states and line moves as plain values (Payload) and checks them:
- in the project, a writer makes no state; its config moves no line; its
  line.create makes only the one new save-back line it names;
- in its overlays, a writer's states are on the lines the record moves;
- no record of a limited machine carries queue_change, ref_change or
  attestation, and its machine record makes no state and moves no line.

rules() collected trusts and delegations of a signer after its untrust. Now
the untrusts are decided first, in time order, each with the untrusts before
it, and a trust or delegation counts only when its signer was not untrusted at
or before its time.

Fixes #348

